@page
@model ProjectManagement.Areas.Admin.Pages.Help.IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Administration guide";
}

<partial name="~/Areas/Admin/Pages/Shared/_AdminPageHeader.cshtml" model="Model.Header" />

<div class="admin-guide-layout">
    <div class="admin-guide-sections">
        @* Short answers first (docs/ux/admin-module.md, PR 8); the full guide follows. *@
        <section id="how-do-i" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section admin-how-do-i" aria-labelledby="how-do-i-title">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><h2 id="how-do-i-title">How do I…</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-signpost-split" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <dl class="admin-how-do-i__list">
                @foreach (var answer in Model.Answers)
                {
                    <div>
                        <dt>@answer.Question</dt>
                        <dd>
                            @answer.Answer
                            @if (answer.Href is not null)
                            {
                                <a href="@answer.Href">@answer.LinkText <i class="bi bi-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                            }
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                }
            </dl>
        </section>

        <section id="people-access" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">People</div><h2>Accounts, from creation to deletion</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-people" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body">
                <p>Use <strong>Disable</strong> when sign-in must stop while records, ownership and attribution remain intact. Password reset issues a temporary credential, signs out open sessions at their next check (every minute by default, <code>Security:SessionRevalidationMinutes</code>) and requires a change at the next sign-in. Disabling an account or changing its roles reaches open sessions the same way.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Review the complete account page before changing privileged roles.</li>
                    <li>Do not disable or remove the final active Administrator account.</li>
                    <li>Use deletion only when the lifecycle and retention safeguards permit it.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="access-governance" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">People</div><h2>Who has which role</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-shield-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body">
                <p>Who has which role shows which role grants each admin job, and which admin and HoD accounts need a look.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>What each role can do is set in PRISM itself; this page shows it but cannot change it. To change what a person can do, change their roles on Users.</li>
                    <li>Disabled or deletion-pending accounts may retain role assignments for historical and restoration purposes.</li>
                    <li>Maintain more than one active Administrator where organisational policy permits.</li>
                    <li>Export the access review file for a formal review or your records.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="monitoring" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">Sign-ins &amp; audit</div><h2>Sign-in activity, the audit log and ERP usage</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-graph-up-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body">
                <p>Sign-in activity is for security; ERP usage shows how much PRISM is used. A person can stay signed in for several days, so the number of sign-ins does not show daily use.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>ERP usage records which pages people open and when they are active. It never records keystrokes, page content or search text.</li>
                    <li>Approximate active time is an adoption indicator, not attendance or individual performance.</li>
                    <li>Failed sign-ins and lockouts are listed in Sign-in activity; review them there.</li>
                    <li>System health checks that PRISM is ready. A check that has not run yet is not the same as OK.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="recovery" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">Restore &amp; archive</div><h2>Archiving, deleting and restoring</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-arrow-counterclockwise" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body">
                <p><strong>Archive</strong> takes a record out of everyday lists; nothing is deleted. <strong>Delete</strong> moves it to Restore deleted items, where it can be brought back until its time is up. <strong>Purge</strong> deletes it for good, with its stored files, and cannot be undone.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Review dependent records and storage impact before permanent deletion.</li>
                    <li>Before deleting for good, PRISM asks you to type the exact name and confirm.</li>
                    <li>Purging by hand and the automatic purge when time is up follow the same checks.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="maintenance" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">System</div><h2>Data jobs</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-tools" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body">
                <p>Before you use Copy PDFs into the repository, check its last run on that page. A run starts at once, skips files already in the repository and finishes even if you leave the page. Legacy project import must be checked and previewed before it saves anything, so the same file cannot be imported twice by mistake.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="master-data" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">Reference lists</div><h2>Lists used in forms</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-sliders2" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body">
                <p>These lists are the choices offered in forms across PRISM. A change shows in forms at once and in reports on past records.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Deactivate referenced values instead of deleting them.</li>
                    <li>Category deletion is permitted only when no projects, children or descendants depend on the entry.</li>
                    <li>Moving a value changes only the order forms show it in; records that use it do not change.</li>
                    <li>Celebrations are entered on their own page; they are not taken from user accounts.</li>
                    <li>Every add, edit, deactivate, move and delete is written to the audit log.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

                <section id="office-calendar" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header"><div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">Reference lists</div><h2>Gazetted and restricted holidays</h2></div><i class="bi bi-calendar-week" aria-hidden="true"></i></header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body"><p>Classification and office observance are separate decisions. Every Restricted Holiday appears on the shared calendar, but only Gazetted Holidays and RHs declared as office holidays close the office and affect future working-day calculations.</p><ul><li>Use <strong>Declare as office holiday</strong> to observe an RH office-wide.</li><li>Use <strong>Withdraw office observance</strong> to return the date to normal working status while retaining the RH for information.</li><li>Existing approved project dates are never silently recalculated.</li></ul></div>
        </section>

        <section id="configuration-integrity" class="admin-panel admin-guide-section">
            <header class="admin-panel__header">
                <div><div class="admin-panel__eyebrow">System</div><h2>Data checks</h2></div>
                <i class="bi bi-clipboard2-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </header>
            <div class="admin-guide-section__body">
                <p>Data checks looks for problems in the lists (categories inside themselves, repeated names, missing links, repeated order numbers). Looking changes nothing.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>The only automatic fix is renumbering a list's order.</li>
                    <li>Other problems need you to open the list and fix the value yourself.</li>
                    <li>Every fix is written to the audit log: which list, how many values and who.</li>
                    <li>Run Data checks after a legacy import or a big change to the categories.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="admin-panel admin-guide-nav" aria-label="Guide sections">
        <header class="admin-panel__header"><div><h2>On this page</h2></div></header>
        <a href="#how-do-i">How do I…</a>
        <a href="#people-access">Accounts</a>
        <a href="#access-governance">Who has which role</a>
        <a href="#monitoring">Sign-ins and audit</a>
        <a href="#recovery">Archiving, deleting and restoring</a>
        <a href="#maintenance">Data jobs</a>
        <a href="#master-data">Lists used in forms</a>
        <a href="#office-calendar">Holidays</a>
        <a href="#configuration-integrity">Data checks</a>
    </aside>
</div>

@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/js/admin/admin-help.js" asp-append-version="true" defer></script>
}
